{
  "case_id": "2024-24a884",
  "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0000-0006",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:12 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0000-0007",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GEN. D. JOHN SAUER, Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the Applicants."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0000-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "On January 20, 2025, President Trump issued Executive Order 14,160, Protecting the Meaning and Value of American Citizenship. This order reflects the original meaning of the Fourteenth Amendment, which guaranteed citizenship to this children of former slaves, not to illegal aliens or temporary visitors."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0000-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Since January 20, district courts have now issued 40 universal injunctions against the federal government, including 35 from the same five"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Sauer",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Universal injunctions exceed the judicial power granted in Article III, which exists only to address the injury to the complaining party. They transgress the traditional bounds of equitable authority, and they create a host of practical problems."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Sauer",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0000-0003",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "They increase the pressures on this Court's emergency docket."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: General Sauer, the -- these universal injunctions, as you say, have proliferated over the last three decades or so. Would you discuss, though, the origins of universal injunctions? In particular, I'm interested in sort of historical analogues or the historical pedigree, particularly the bill of peace that -- that was proffered by Respondents."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Sauer",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "First of all, it's not necessary to provide complete relief to the plaintiffs. What we offered, for example, in the District of Massachusetts in the Seconds or the First Circuit was an injunction that would enjoin the federal officials and order them to treat the people who would otherwise be covered by the Executive Order as eligible for the services that result in the pocketbook injuries to the states."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Sauer",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the states have to be provided complete relief because of interstate travel and patchwork. I think that's very effectively responded to by Chief Judge Sutton's opinion in the Second Circuit, where he says this is a problem."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And then, with respect to class certification, your -- your friends on the other side point out that that takes time, and there are, as you've emphasized, hurdles that have to be met to achieve class certification."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Sauer",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It may be appropriate -- we do not concede that it's appropriate in this case, but it may be appropriate in other cases."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Sauer",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "All the --it -- that's exactly correct. The Court does not have to rest on Article III because the Court could say, and as we've argued and as Justice Thomas's separate opinion in Trump against Hawaii says, the 1789 Judiciary Act, when it said suits in equity are what the federal courts can do, had nothing like this in mind."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Sauer",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0001-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Rule 23 would be one natural path, assuming that a class could be certified, which we might dispute in this particular case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Sauer",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0001-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "That would be a profoundly wrong result. But I think what I would offer is that, very similar to Labrador against Poe, what the Court should be engaging in here is a balancing of the equitable factors as to the scope of remedial relief, not as to the underlying merits."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0001-0010",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Does the government commit to not applying its EO in the entire Second Circuit, or does it say, no, we can continue to apply the rule as to everybody else in the Second Circuit?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Sauer",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0001-0011",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I can't answer because it would depend on what the lower court decision said."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0001-0014",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "General, when were the first universal injunctions used?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0001-0016",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If we were to hold that the states have standing and if it is possible for a plaintiff to get emergency certification of a class, would we -- suppose we agreed with you on universal injunctions but allowed those other two avenues. Would those -- would the practical problem be rectified to any substantial degree?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Sauer",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0001-0017",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I -- I -- I disagree with that profoundly."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Sauer",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0001-0020",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "No party has asked for that in this case, and I think one reason is that would deny the Court of the benefit of percolation and multiple lower courts of a novel and sensitive and important constitutional question."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: -- and there were some people in Congress who argued against the Thirteenth Amendment just because of that, some people who argued against passing the amendment just because of that, because it would give citizenship to gypsies."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "U.S. Government",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL SAUER: I think the relevant history of the Fourteenth Amendment is the statements of Senator Trumbull, who emphasized that domicile was the key criteria, and he said that in a letter to Andrew Jackson, and there -- we've cited in our Ninth Circuit briefing --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: So, General, on this question of expedition, I mean, it -- it sort of depends on the government's own actions in a case like this one, where one can expect that there is not going to be a great deal of disagreement among the lower courts."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: If you win this challenge and say there is no nationwide injunction and it all has to be through individual cases, then I can't see how an individual who is not, you know, being treated equivalently to the individual who brought the case would have any ability to bring the substantive question to us."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0002-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: So the technical problem here seems to be class-wide relief without the district courts going through the steps to assess whether a class should be certified, correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "U.S. Government",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0002-0009",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL SAUER: There may be problems of commonality and typicality, for example. For -- for example, there's two different sets of groups that are affected by the Executive Order. There are those where the mothers are temporarily present and those where the mother are illegally present, and in both cases, the father is neither a citizen nor a lawful permanent resident."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0002-0010",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: And you think, I think you just said, it's very possible that class certification may be granted?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "U.S. Government",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0002-0011",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL SAUER: Yeah, we -- we do set aside that issue if I may."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0002-0012",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: I want to ask one thing about something in your brief. You said: \"And, of course, this Court's decisions constitute controlling precedent throughout the nation. If this Court were to hold a challenged statute or policy unconstitutional, the government could not successfully enforce it against anyone, party or not, in light of stare decisis.\" You agree with that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "U.S. Government",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0002-0015",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL SAUER: Such as they could require a showing of, you know, documentation showing legal presence in the country. For a temporary visitor, for example, they could see whether they're on a B-1 visa, which would exclude kind of the birthright citizenship in that kind of --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "U.S. Government",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0002-0019",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 62,
        "start": 62
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL SAUER: Our general practice is to respect those precedents, but there are circumstances when it is not a categorical practice. It is -- and that is not a new policy."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "U.S. Government",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0002-0021",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL SAUER: We do think percolation is really important for this one."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: But the government's done that in other cases too, right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Sauer",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0003-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 70,
        "start": 70
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "SO, AS FAR AS I CAN TELL, YOUR BOTTOM LINE SEEMS TO BE THAT WHAT YOU CALL UNIVERSAL INJUNCTIONS GIVE RELIEF TO NONPARTIES WITHOUT GOING THROUGH THE NECESSARY STEPS, WHICH YOU IDENTIFY IN RULE 23."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 85,
        "start": 85
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Can I ask you a question about that, counsel? Your three buckets are very thoughtful."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice GORSUCH",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0004-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 93,
        "start": 93
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "How would you get this -- how would you get the merits of this case to us promptly?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Heritage Reporting Corporation",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0004-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 98,
        "start": 98
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I do think presidents of both parties have objected to nationwide injunctions."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Heritage Reporting Corporation",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0004-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 100,
        "start": 100
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We have never believed, even as nationwide injunctions restrained policies that we favored, that they were categorically off the table. We've always taken the position that they are sometimes available in narrow circumstances, whether we like the policy or don't like the policy."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0005-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 109,
        "start": 109
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In equity, correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Heritage Reporting Corporation",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0005-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 110,
        "start": 110
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So say that there's an Executive Order that says: We're just not going to count minors, people under 18, in apportionment anymore; we're only going to count people who are voting age. And the State of New York files a lawsuit, and it wins its lawsuit, and all of its 17-and-under-year-olds get counted for apportionment."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Heritage Reporting Corporation",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0005-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 111,
        "start": 111
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "That isn't indivisible in any way. It's not a redistricting plan. It's not a power plant. But it is going to skew apportionment in a way that is totally unfair practically and legally to third parties because now 17-year-olds are being counted in New York, but they're not being counted in Oklahoma. And you would end up messing up apportionment between states for that very reason. And that shows as just a broader insight that we've always looked to the harms that third parties will suffer as negative externalities of court orders."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Heritage Reporting Corporation",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0005-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 120,
        "start": 120
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think what you could say is, here, there were two sentences in an emergency application that raise new alternative ways to remedy the harms."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Heritage Reporting Corporation",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0005-0004",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 127,
        "start": 127
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "prevent the catastrophic consequences that will result for the plaintiffs and our country if the government is allowed to execute an unconstitutional citizenship-stripping scheme"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Heritage Reporting Corporation",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0005-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 127,
        "start": 127
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The government is wrong. It is well settled that preliminary injunctions may benefit nonparties when necessary to provide complete relief to the plaintiffs or when warranted by extraordinary circumstances, both of which are true here."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0005-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 128,
        "start": 128
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "You say the government is wrong about the availability of preliminary injunctions. On what do you base that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Heritage Reporting Corporation",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0005-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 128,
        "start": 128
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think the two reasons I identified, one, it is well settled, and I understood General Sauer to agree today, that universal injunctive relief is appropriate when necessary to provide complete relief to the plaintiffs. That is the case here, and I'm happy to talk about that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Corkran",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0006-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 129,
        "start": 129
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. CORKRAN: So I -- you know, again, I would put us in the complete relief bucket."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0006-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 129,
        "start": 129
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In 2017, the Rules Committee considered a proposal from Professor Bray to amend the rule to prohibit relief to nonparties. The committee rejected that proposal because it found that it ran afoul of"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0006-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 146,
        "start": 146
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: I find it hard to understand how a district court, in looking at a preliminary injunction under the Winter factors, where we said that the likelihood of success on the merits is the keystone, how we could separate that out and say the keystone of whether you're entitled to universal injunction is the only merits question because the other factors are not eliminated by Winter."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Corkran",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0007-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 150,
        "start": 150
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the government's proposal of channeling through Rule 23 does nothing to solve anything you just described."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0007-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 151,
        "start": 151
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Some of your concerns about this Court being involved, I guess I'm not sure I really understand that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Professor Pfander",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0007-0003",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 157,
        "start": 157
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think Professor Pfander's amicus brief is really helpful on that. He talks about the -- the patent laws."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Corkran",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0007-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 158,
        "start": 158
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think Rule 71 contemplates that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 0.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
